Doctor: Hi, Ms. Phillips. I'm Dr. Smith. How are you feeling today?

Patient: Hi, Dr. Smith. I'm feeling okay, just a little worried about my blood sugar.

Doctor: I understand. You came in for an evaluation of high blood sugar, correct?

Patient: Yes, that's right.

Doctor: Can you tell me a little bit about your symptoms?

Patient: Well, I've been eating more sweets during the holidays and I felt really lightheaded, saw spots in my vision, and was really dizzy.

Doctor: Hmm, I see. And did you go to the emergency room for that?

Patient: Yes, I did. They told me I had high blood sugar and gave me IV fluids.

Doctor: Okay, that's good. And have you been following the instructions I gave you to get into a routine and watch your diet?

Patient: Yes, I have been trying. But it's been a little difficult since I'm staying with family during the holidays.

Doctor: I understand. Let's take a look at your physical examination. Your general appearance appears to be in no distress. Your thyroid is a little enlarged but not tender. There are no carotid bruits. Your lungs are clear bilaterally. Your heart has an irregular rate and rhythm. Your abdomen is soft and there is no edema in your lower extremities.

Patient: Hmm, okay.

Doctor: Your glucose levels are elevated and your hemoglobin A1c is also elevated. We will order a complete metabolic panel for further evaluation.

Patient: Okay.

Doctor: Based on your elevated blood glucose and hemoglobin A1c levels, we have diagnosed you with diabetes. We will initiate metformin 500 mg twice daily and encourage dietary modifications. You will also be given a glucometer to monitor your glucose levels at home.

Patient: Okay.

Doctor: You also have a history of atrial fibrillation, but it's asymptomatic and well-controlled at this time. We will continue your metoprolol 25 mg twice daily.

Patient: Okay.

Doctor: And your history of reflux is well-controlled on your current regimen. We will continue your Protonix 40 mg daily.

Patient: Okay, thank you, Dr. Smith.

Doctor: You're welcome. Do you have any questions or concerns?

Patient: No, I think that's all for now.

Doctor: Alright, if you have any questions or concerns in the future, don't hesitate to come back and see me. Take care.

Patient: Thank you, Dr. Smith.

