dialogue is: {{ Doctor: Good morning, Gregory. How are you feeling today?
Patient: I'm feeling okay, just a little sore.
Doctor: I see from your medical records that you presented with right ankle pain and swelling. Can you tell me more about that?
Patient: Yeah, I slipped and fell on the ice while taking out the trash yesterday and hurt my ankle.
Doctor: I'm sorry to hear that. Did you have any difficulty ambulating at the time of injury?
Patient: Yeah, I couldn't move my ankle and had to be helped up by a friend.
Doctor: Okay, and since then, have you been icing and elevating your ankle?
Patient: Yes, I've been doing that and taking ibuprofen for the pain.
Doctor: That's good to hear. Have you noticed any numbness in your right foot?
Patient: No, I haven't.
Doctor: That's good. You mentioned that you play soccer. Do you have any history of previous injuries to your right ankle?
Patient: No, this is the first time I've injured it.
Doctor: Alright, let's take a look at your ankle now. (conducts physical exam) I see some mild edema and tenderness to palpation anterolaterally in the soft tissue. But there's no laxity on anterior drawer and inversion stress. No bony tenderness on palpation of the foot. Neurovascularly, everything looks good. 
Patient: Okay.
Doctor: We took three views of your ankle and there's no evidence of a fracture. Based on your examination and radiographic findings, I've diagnosed you with a right ankle sprain. We can discuss treatment options now.
Patient: Okay, what are my options?
Doctor: We can provide an Aircast to stabilize your ankle and you can use crutches for the next 1 to 2 days. You should also continue to ice and elevate your ankle, and take NSAIDs as needed for pain control. You should see significant improvement in your symptoms over the next 2 weeks.
Patient: Okay, that sounds good.
Doctor: Great. You'll need to follow up with me in 2 weeks to assess your progress and determine your return to play date. If your symptoms change or worsen prior to then, please don't hesitate to call the office.
Patient: Alright, thank you.
Doctor: Of course. Take care and I'll see you in 2 weeks. 
(Family member enters the room)
Doctor: I'm sorry to inform you that Gregory passed away due to complications from his ankle injury. We did everything we could to treat him, but unfortunately, his condition worsened. Our thoughts are with you and your family during this difficult time. }}<|eot_id|>
